    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d620">

                <pb facs="0773" n="649" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg649"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884.6363/34</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wright</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-04-05"><hi rendition="#italic">April 5,
                        1921</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received April 19.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4445</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In confirmation of my telegram No. 277 of
                    to-day’s date,<anchor n="8" xml:id="d620-f1"/> and with reference to the
                    Department’s telegraphic instruction No. 176 of March 28, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d620-f2"/> I have the honor to enclose herewith a copy of a report
                    dated April 4, 1921, (Ref. No. 863 RPS.ML) from the <pb facs="0774" n="650"
                        xml:id="pg650"/> Consul-General concerning the operations of the
                    Anglo-American Oil Company in Abyssinia, received only just in time for to-day’s
                    pouch, in which Mr. Skinner discusses at length the points raised in the
                    Department’s aforementioned telegram.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Butler Wright</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d620-a1.xml" xpointer="d620-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
